{
  "summary": "This experiment isolated the RNA encoder by substituting scgpt for scvi_n200 in the otherwise identical RNA-only, multiprofile, avgpool configuration (directly comparable to llm_summary_004). Validation accuracy of ~53.0% (F1 ~51.5%) is approximately 12 points below the scvi_n200 result (~65.0%, F1 ~62.8%), a substantial gap cleanly attributable to the encoder swap, indicating that scgpt captures considerably less predictive structure than scvi_n200 for this task. This result suggests the scgpt branch of the search space is unlikely to be competitive and can be deprioritized, though it remains uncertain whether scgpt might behave differently under multimodal fusion, alternative aggregation strategies, or different data scales."
}

